        {
          "text": "**The Hertzsprung-Russell (H-R) Diagram:** This is the *single most important graph* in stellar astrophysics, but it can be understood entirely conceptually. It's a \"map\" that plots a star's brightness against its temperature, revealing the main sequence, giants, and dwarfs as distinct families.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 102,
          "source": "topic-set-the-life-and-influence-of-stars-🆔20251106222139.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Binary Star Systems:** Exploring how stars co-evolve when they are gravitationally bound to a partner. This leads to unique phenomena like certain types of supernovae and the transfer of mass between stars.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 109,
          "source": "topic-set-the-life-and-influence-of-stars-🆔20251106222139.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Stellar Classification (O-B-A-F-G-K-M):** The system (developed by Annie Jump Cannon) for categorizing stars by their spectral \"fingerprints,\" which is fundamentally a classification by temperature and color.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 120,
          "source": "topic-set-the-life-and-influence-of-stars-🆔20251106222139.md"
        }
      ]
